// mesh:app — a resilience playground in front of a deliberately flaky upstream.
//
// Every service that calls another service needs the same three behaviours, and
// almost every codebase re-invents them inline, differently, per call site:
//
//   * RETRY with exponential backoff + jitter — ride out a blip.
//   * a CIRCUIT BREAKER — stop dialling an upstream that is already down, so the
//     caller fails fast instead of piling threads onto a corpse.
//   * an SLO — "too slow" is a failure, not a success that happens to be late.
//
// The ALGORITHMS are the stateless `resilience:breaker` component. The DURABILITY
// is this domain's per-key circuit record in `records:store`, updated under a
// revision compare-and-set so concurrent callers converge on one circuit (the
// same shape `gate:app` uses for rate-limit state — see docs/apps/GATE.md). The upstream
// hop is a REAL outgoing HTTP request through `proxy:route`, so a tripped
// breaker is observably a request that never leaves the host.
//
// The demo upstream (examples/mesh, `just mesh-upstream`) fails on demand:
// `/upstream/hit?fail=1` answers 500, `?delay=400` answers slowly, and killing
// it entirely gives a real connect-refused. Nothing is simulated in here.
//
// No auth: a playground keys circuits by a client-supplied name.
//
// Routes (under /api so the static SPA fallback leaves them alone):
//   POST /api/call {key, path?, ...policy}   guarded call -> 200 / 502 / 503
//   GET  /api/circuit/{key}                  one circuit's state + counters
//   GET  /api/circuits                       every circuit (the dashboard)
//   POST /api/reset {key}                    forget a circuit
package mesh:app@0.1.0;

/// The resilience gateway — retry + circuit breaker + SLO over a real upstream.
world mesh-domain {
    export wasi:http/incoming-handler@0.2.0;

    // the durable per-key circuit state (breaker memory that survives restarts).
    import records:store/store@0.1.0;
    // the stateless algorithms: breaker state machine + backoff schedule.
    import resilience:breaker/breaker@0.1.0;
    // the real outgoing HTTP hop to the upstream (route table from wasi:config).
    import proxy:route/router@0.1.0;
    // state timestamps (unix millis).
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;
    // call latency + the backoff sleep between attempts.
    import wasi:clocks/monotonic-clock@0.2.0;
}
